<title>USA: USDA donates wheat to Kyrgyzstan.</title>
<headline>USDA donates wheat to Kyrgyzstan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday it would donate about 7,000 tonnes of wheat to Agricultural Cooperative Development International to support economic development initiatives in Kyrgyzstan.</p>
<p>The U.S.-based charity may sell wheat in that country and use the proceeds for grants and loans to small agribusiness enterprises and other development activities, USDA said.</p>
<p>The supply period for the donation is fiscal year 1996.</p>
</text>
